    <entry>
      <title>Slack Protocol Handler</title>
      <link href="/2026/11/19/slack-protocol-handler/"/>
      <url>/2026/11/19/slack-protocol-handler/</url>
      
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>e.g. SetWindowOpenHandler</p><p><img src="/images/slack-protocol-handler/image.png"></p><p>Deep link handling works as shown above.</p><p>eR: the HANDLE_DEEP_LINK action creator.</p><p>It builds an action (<code>payload: { url }</code>), which is then consumed by 1 reducer + 5 epics.</p><h4 id="Reducer"><a href="#Reducer" class="headerlink" title="Reducer"></a>Reducer</h4><p><img src="/images/slack-protocol-handler/image-1.png"></p><p>It reads the <code>?team=</code> value from the deep link, and only when that team already exists in the list of logged-in workspaces (<code>teamsByIndex</code>) does it change <code>selectedTeamId</code> to that team, switching the workspace shown on screen.</p><p>If there is no <code>team</code> parameter, or the team is unknown, it leaves the state as is (no-op). In other words, the reducer is a pure state change that only “switches focus to the team the deep link points to”; the actual side effects (settings &#x2F; app actions &#x2F; forwarding to the webapp) are handled by the epics.</p><h4 id="Epics"><a href="#Epics" class="headerlink" title="Epics"></a>Epics</h4><ol><li>FORWARD_DEEP_LINK_TO_WEBAPP</li></ol><figure class="highlight jsx"><table><tr><td class="gutter"><pre><span class="line">1</span><br><span class="line">2</span><br><span class="line">3</span><br><span class="line">4</span><br><span class="line">5</span><br><span class="line">6</span><br></pre></td><td class="code"><pre><span class="line">dd = <span class="title function_">e3</span>(n9.<span class="property">FORWARD_DEEP_LINK_TO_WEBAPP</span>, <span class="function">(<span class="params">e, t</span>) =&gt;</span></span><br><span class="line">  <span class="title function_">ax</span>(e, t).<span class="title function_">pipe</span>(</span><br><span class="line">    <span class="title function_">ow</span>(n9.<span class="property">FORWARD_DEEP_LINK_TO_WEBAPP</span>),</span><br><span class="line">    (<span class="number">0</span>, eZ.<span class="property">filter</span>)(<span class="function">(<span class="params">&#123; args: &#123; team: e &#125; &#125;</span>) =&gt;</span></span><br><span class="line">      <span class="title function_">du</span>(e, t.<span class="property">value</span>.<span class="property">workspaces</span>),</span><br><span class="line">      <span class="comment">// ...</span></span><br></pre></td></tr></table></figure><p>Handles the case where <code>team</code> is empty or is an already logged-in workspace. It finds the already-loaded webapp renderer for that workspace and passes the deep link over IPC (<code>FORWARD_DEEP_LINK</code>) so the in-app logic can handle things like channel&#x2F;message navigation.</p><ol start="2"><li>TRANSFORM_DEEP_LINKS</li></ol><figure class="highlight jsx"><table><tr><td class="gutter"><pre><span class="line">1</span><br><span class="line">2</span><br><span class="line">3</span><br><span class="line">4</span><br><span class="line">5</span><br><span class="line">6</span><br><span class="line">7</span><br></pre></td><td class="code"><pre><span class="line">dp = <span class="title function_">e3</span>(n9.<span class="property">TRANSFORM_DEEP_LINKS</span>, <span class="function">(<span class="params">e, t</span>) =&gt;</span></span><br><span class="line">  <span class="title function_">ax</span>(e, t).<span class="title function_">pipe</span>(</span><br><span class="line">    <span class="title function_">ow</span>(n9.<span class="property">TRANSFORM_DEEP_LINKS</span>),</span><br><span class="line">    (<span class="number">0</span>, eZ.<span class="property">filter</span>)(</span><br><span class="line">      <span class="function">(<span class="params">&#123; args: &#123; team: e &#125; &#125;</span>) =&gt;</span> !<span class="title function_">du</span>(e, t.<span class="property">value</span>.<span class="property">workspaces</span>),</span><br><span class="line">    ),</span><br><span class="line">    <span class="comment">// ...</span></span><br></pre></td></tr></table></figure><p>Handles the case where a <code>team</code> is present but not yet logged in (unknown). It reverse-searches the workspaces I’m logged into for one that contains that team (preferring the currently selected workspace, otherwise scanning all of them). If found, it reassembles the deep link URL for that workspace (<code>slack://&lt;cmd&gt;?team=&lt;resolved team&gt;&amp;...</code>) and dispatches it back through <code>eR</code>.</p><ol start="3"><li>UPDATE_SETTINGS_VIA_DEEP_LINKS</li></ol><figure class="highlight jsx"><table><tr><td class="gutter"><pre><span class="line">1</span><br><span class="line">2</span><br><span class="line">3</span><br><span class="line">4</span><br><span class="line">5</span><br><span class="line">6</span><br><span class="line">7</span><br><span class="line">8</span><br><span class="line">9</span><br><span class="line">10</span><br><span class="line">11</span><br><span class="line">12</span><br><span class="line">13</span><br><span class="line">14</span><br><span class="line">15</span><br><span class="line">16</span><br><span class="line">17</span><br><span class="line">18</span><br><span class="line">19</span><br><span class="line">20</span><br><span class="line">21</span><br><span class="line">22</span><br><span class="line">23</span><br></pre></td><td class="code"><pre><span class="line">dg = <span class="title function_">e3</span>(n9.<span class="property">UPDATE_SETTINGS_VIA_DEEP_LINKS</span>, <span class="function">(<span class="params">e</span>) =&gt;</span></span><br><span class="line">  e.<span class="title function_">pipe</span>(</span><br><span class="line">    <span class="title function_">n8</span>(eR), <span class="comment">// only let HANDLE_DEEP_LINK actions through</span></span><br><span class="line">    <span class="title function_">ow</span>(n9.<span class="property">UPDATE_SETTINGS_VIA_DEEP_LINKS</span>), <span class="comment">// extract args for this epic</span></span><br><span class="line">    <span class="title function_">dh</span>(),  <span class="comment">// parse the settings payload: pull JSON out of the url into an object</span></span><br><span class="line">    (<span class="number">0</span>, eZ.<span class="property">map</span>)(<span class="function">(<span class="params">e</span>) =&gt;</span></span><br><span class="line">      (<span class="keyword">function</span> (<span class="params">e</span>) &#123;</span><br><span class="line">        <span class="keyword">let</span> t = (<span class="number">0</span>, ep.<span class="property">A</span>)(e, f7); <span class="comment">// pick only keys in the f7 allowlist (32 keys)</span></span><br><span class="line">        <span class="keyword">if</span> (<span class="number">0</span> === <span class="title class_">Object</span>.<span class="title function_">keys</span>(t).<span class="property">length</span>) <span class="keyword">return</span> &#123;&#125;; <span class="comment">// drop if no allowed keys</span></span><br><span class="line">        <span class="keyword">let</span> &#123; <span class="attr">error</span>: r &#125; = dl.<span class="title function_">validate</span>(t); <span class="comment">// validate values</span></span><br><span class="line">        <span class="keyword">return</span> r</span><br><span class="line">          ? (eq.<span class="property">vF</span>.<span class="title function_">error</span>(<span class="string">&quot;Validation failed:&quot;</span>, r.<span class="property">details</span>), &#123;&#125;) <span class="comment">// bad value -&gt; drop</span></span><br><span class="line">          : (t.<span class="property">releaseChannelOverride</span> &amp;&amp;</span><br><span class="line">                !<span class="title class_">Object</span>.<span class="title function_">values</span>(e9.<span class="property">Xp</span>).<span class="title function_">includes</span>(t.<span class="property">releaseChannelOverride</span>)) <span class="comment">// channel not a valid enum</span></span><br><span class="line">            || t.<span class="property">clientEnvironment</span> <span class="comment">// or clientEnvironment is present</span></span><br><span class="line">            ? &#123;&#125; <span class="comment">// deny</span></span><br><span class="line">            : t; <span class="comment">// return only settings that passed</span></span><br><span class="line">      &#125;)(e),</span><br><span class="line">    ),</span><br><span class="line">    (<span class="number">0</span>, eZ.<span class="property">filter</span>)(<span class="function">(<span class="params">e</span>) =&gt;</span> <span class="title class_">Object</span>.<span class="title function_">keys</span>(e).<span class="property">length</span> &gt; <span class="number">0</span>), <span class="comment">// stop if empty</span></span><br><span class="line">    <span class="title function_">ie</span>(<span class="function">(<span class="params">e</span>) =&gt;</span> <span class="title function_">of</span>(e), n9.<span class="property">UPDATE_SETTINGS_VIA_DEEP_LINKS</span>), <span class="comment">// of(settings) = dispatch UPDATE_SETTINGS -&gt; actually apply</span></span><br><span class="line">  ),</span><br><span class="line">)</span><br></pre></td></tr></table></figure><p>→ Settings are applied after only passing through the allowlist + value validation. If <code>clientEnvironment</code> is included, it returns an empty dist entirely. (Covered in SWITCH_CLIENT_FEATURE_MODE_VIA_DEEP_LINKS.)</p><p>It directly sets f7 settings such as <code>launchOnStartup</code>, <code>startNetLogAtLaunch</code>, <code>releaseChannelOverride</code>.</p><ul><li><p>dh()</p>  <figure class="highlight jsx"><table><tr><td class="gutter"><pre><span class="line">1</span><br><span class="line">2</span><br><span class="line">3</span><br><span class="line">4</span><br><span class="line">5</span><br><span class="line">6</span><br><span class="line">7</span><br><span class="line">8</span><br><span class="line">9</span><br><span class="line">10</span><br><span class="line">11</span><br><span class="line">12</span><br><span class="line">13</span><br><span class="line">14</span><br></pre></td><td class="code"><pre><span class="line">dh = <span class="function">() =&gt;</span> <span class="function">(<span class="params">e</span>) =&gt;</span></span><br><span class="line">  e.<span class="title function_">pipe</span>(</span><br><span class="line">    (<span class="number">0</span>, eZ.<span class="property">filter</span>)(<span class="function">(<span class="params">&#123; payload: e &#125;</span>) =&gt;</span> <span class="title function_">i8</span>(e.<span class="property">url</span>)), <span class="comment">// is the url a &quot;settings deep link&quot;?</span></span><br><span class="line">    (<span class="number">0</span>, eZ.<span class="property">map</span>)(<span class="function">(<span class="params">&#123; payload: e &#125;</span>) =&gt;</span> (<span class="number">0</span>, tT.<span class="property">QW</span>)(e.<span class="property">url</span>)), <span class="comment">// extract the settings JSON &#x27;string&#x27; from the url (QW)</span></span><br><span class="line">    (<span class="number">0</span>, eZ.<span class="property">map</span>)(<span class="function">(<span class="params">e</span>) =&gt;</span></span><br><span class="line">      (<span class="keyword">function</span> (<span class="params">e</span>) &#123;</span><br><span class="line">        <span class="keyword">let</span> t = &#123;&#125;;</span><br><span class="line">        <span class="keyword">try</span> &#123; t = <span class="title class_">JSON</span>.<span class="title function_">parse</span>(e); &#125; <span class="comment">// settings are JSON-parsed</span></span><br><span class="line">        <span class="keyword">catch</span> (e) &#123; eq.<span class="property">vF</span>.<span class="title function_">warn</span>(<span class="string">&quot;...Failed to parse settings update json.&quot;</span>); &#125;</span><br><span class="line">        <span class="keyword">return</span> t;</span><br><span class="line">      &#125;)(e),</span><br><span class="line">    ),</span><br><span class="line">    (<span class="number">0</span>, eZ.<span class="property">filter</span>)(<span class="function">(<span class="params">e</span>) =&gt;</span> !!e),</span><br><span class="line">  )</span><br></pre></td></tr></table></figure><p>  It parses the value from a single <code>?update=&lt;JSON&gt;</code> parameter.</p><p>  e.g. <code>slack://settings?update={&quot;startNetLogAtLaunch&quot;:true,&quot;runFromTray&quot;:false}</code></p></li></ul><ol start="4"><li>SWITCH_CLIENT_FEATURE_MODE_VIA_DEEP_LINKS</li></ol><figure class="highlight jsx"><table><tr><td class="gutter"><pre><span class="line">1</span><br><span class="line">2</span><br><span class="line">3</span><br><span class="line">4</span><br><span class="line">5</span><br><span class="line">6</span><br><span class="line">7</span><br><span class="line">8</span><br><span class="line">9</span><br><span class="line">10</span><br><span class="line">11</span><br><span class="line">12</span><br><span class="line">13</span><br><span class="line">14</span><br></pre></td><td class="code"><pre><span class="line">dE = <span class="title function_">e3</span>(n9.<span class="property">SWITCH_CLIENT_FEATURE_MODE_VIA_DEEP_LINKS</span>, <span class="function">(<span class="params">e</span>) =&gt;</span></span><br><span class="line">  e.<span class="title function_">pipe</span>(</span><br><span class="line">    <span class="title function_">n8</span>(eR), <span class="title function_">ow</span>(...), <span class="title function_">dh</span>(), <span class="comment">// HANDLE_DEEP_LINK + parse settings JSON</span></span><br><span class="line">    (<span class="number">0</span>, eZ.<span class="property">map</span>)(<span class="function">(<span class="params">e</span>) =&gt;</span> &#123;</span><br><span class="line">      <span class="keyword">if</span> (<span class="number">1</span> !== <span class="title class_">Object</span>.<span class="title function_">keys</span>(e ?? &#123;&#125;).<span class="property">length</span> || !e.<span class="property">clientEnvironment</span>)</span><br><span class="line">        <span class="keyword">return</span> <span class="literal">null</span>; <span class="comment">// only when clientEnvironment is the single key</span></span><br><span class="line">      <span class="keyword">let</span> t = <span class="built_in">parseInt</span>(e.<span class="property">clientEnvironment</span>, <span class="number">10</span>);</span><br><span class="line">      <span class="keyword">return</span> <span class="title class_">Object</span>.<span class="title function_">values</span>(tI.<span class="property">n</span>).<span class="title function_">includes</span>(t) ? t : <span class="literal">null</span>; <span class="comment">// is it a valid enum (NORMAL/RESTRICTED/MILITARY)?</span></span><br><span class="line">    &#125;),</span><br><span class="line">    (<span class="number">0</span>, eZ.<span class="property">filter</span>)(<span class="function">(<span class="params">e</span>) =&gt;</span> !!e &amp;&amp; e !== (<span class="number">0</span>, tD.<span class="property">FO</span>)()), <span class="comment">// only when valid &amp;&amp; different from current</span></span><br><span class="line">    (<span class="number">0</span>, eZ.<span class="property">tap</span>)(<span class="function">(<span class="params">e</span>) =&gt;</span> t_.<span class="property">f</span>.<span class="title function_">setItem</span>(<span class="string">&quot;clientEnvironment&quot;</span>, e)), <span class="comment">// persist the environment to storage</span></span><br><span class="line">    <span class="title function_">ie</span>(<span class="function">() =&gt;</span> <span class="title function_">eA</span>(), n9.<span class="property">SWITCH_CLIENT_FEATURE_MODE_VIA_DEEP_LINKS</span>), <span class="comment">// eA(): relaunch the app</span></span><br><span class="line">  ),</span><br><span class="line">)</span><br></pre></td></tr></table></figure><p>When <code>clientEnvironment</code> is present on its own, it’s properly handled here. It uses the same <code>dh</code> function to parse.</p><ol start="5"><li>APP_ACTIONS_VIA_DEEP_LINKS</li></ol><figure class="highlight jsx"><table><tr><td class="gutter"><pre><span class="line">1</span><br><span class="line">2</span><br><span class="line">3</span><br><span class="line">4</span><br><span class="line">5</span><br><span class="line">6</span><br><span class="line">7</span><br><span class="line">8</span><br><span class="line">9</span><br><span class="line">10</span><br><span class="line">11</span><br><span class="line">12</span><br><span class="line">13</span><br><span class="line">14</span><br><span class="line">15</span><br><span class="line">16</span><br><span class="line">17</span><br><span class="line">18</span><br><span class="line">19</span><br><span class="line">20</span><br><span class="line">21</span><br><span class="line">22</span><br><span class="line">23</span><br><span class="line">24</span><br><span class="line">25</span><br><span class="line">26</span><br><span class="line">27</span><br><span class="line">28</span><br><span class="line">29</span><br></pre></td><td class="code"><pre><span class="line">dy = <span class="title function_">e3</span>(n9.<span class="property">APP_ACTIONS_VIA_DEEP_LINKS</span>, <span class="function">(<span class="params">e, t</span>) =&gt;</span> &#123;</span><br><span class="line">  <span class="keyword">let</span> r = !<span class="number">1</span>, <span class="comment">// flag to prevent duplicate dialogs</span></span><br><span class="line">    n = &#123; <span class="attr">type</span>:<span class="string">&quot;question&quot;</span>, <span class="attr">title</span>:<span class="string">&quot;Slack&quot;</span>, <span class="attr">buttons</span>:[<span class="string">&quot;Yes&quot;</span>,<span class="string">&quot;No&quot;</span>],</span><br><span class="line">          <span class="attr">message</span>:<span class="string">&quot;This will save a log file to Slack’s download location. Continue?&quot;</span> &#125;;  <span class="comment">// confirm dialog (for REVEAL_LOGS)</span></span><br><span class="line">  <span class="keyword">return</span> e.<span class="title function_">pipe</span>(</span><br><span class="line">    <span class="title function_">n8</span>(eR), <span class="title function_">ow</span>(n9.<span class="property">APP_ACTIONS_VIA_DEEP_LINKS</span>),</span><br><span class="line">    <span class="function">(<span class="params">e</span>) =&gt;</span> e.<span class="title function_">pipe</span>(</span><br><span class="line">      (<span class="number">0</span>, eZ.<span class="property">filter</span>)(<span class="function">(<span class="params">&#123; payload: e &#125;</span>) =&gt;</span> <span class="title function_">i4</span>(e.<span class="property">url</span>)), <span class="comment">// is it an &#x27;app action deep link&#x27; (slack://app?action= form)?</span></span><br><span class="line">      (<span class="number">0</span>, eZ.<span class="property">map</span>)(<span class="function">(<span class="params">&#123; payload: e &#125;</span>) =&gt;</span> (<span class="number">0</span>, tT.<span class="property">hL</span>)(e.<span class="property">url</span>)), <span class="comment">// url -&gt; action enum (hL)</span></span><br><span class="line">    ),</span><br><span class="line">    (<span class="number">0</span>, eZ.<span class="property">filter</span>)(<span class="function">(<span class="params">e</span>) =&gt;</span> !!e),</span><br><span class="line">    (<span class="number">0</span>, eZ.<span class="property">mergeMap</span>)(<span class="function">(<span class="params">e</span>) =&gt;</span> &#123;</span><br><span class="line">      <span class="keyword">if</span> (e != tT.<span class="property">gM</span>.<span class="property">REVEAL_LOGS</span>) <span class="keyword">return</span> (<span class="number">0</span>, eZ.<span class="property">of</span>)(e); <span class="comment">// if not REVEAL_LOGS, just pass through</span></span><br><span class="line">      <span class="keyword">if</span> (r) <span class="keyword">return</span> eZ.<span class="property">EMPTY</span>; <span class="comment">// ignore if a dialog is already open</span></span><br><span class="line">      &#123; r = !<span class="number">0</span>;</span><br><span class="line">        <span class="keyword">let</span> i = <span class="title function_">o4</span>(t.<span class="property">value</span>.<span class="property">windows</span>),</span><br><span class="line">          o = i ? tr.<span class="property">dialog</span>.<span class="title function_">showMessageBox</span>(i, n) <span class="comment">// yes/no modal only for REVEAL_LOGS</span></span><br><span class="line">                : tr.<span class="property">dialog</span>.<span class="title function_">showMessageBox</span>(n);</span><br><span class="line">        <span class="keyword">return</span> (<span class="number">0</span>, eZ.<span class="property">from</span>)(o).<span class="title function_">pipe</span>(</span><br><span class="line">          (<span class="number">0</span>, eZ.<span class="property">tap</span>)(<span class="function">() =&gt;</span> &#123; r = !<span class="number">1</span>; &#125;),</span><br><span class="line">          (<span class="number">0</span>, eZ.<span class="property">filter</span>)(<span class="function">(<span class="params">&#123; response: e &#125;</span>) =&gt;</span> <span class="number">0</span> === e), <span class="comment">// only pass yes (button 0)</span></span><br><span class="line">          (<span class="number">0</span>, eZ.<span class="property">mapTo</span>)(e),</span><br><span class="line">        );</span><br><span class="line">      &#125;</span><br><span class="line">    &#125;),</span><br><span class="line">    (<span class="number">0</span>, eZ.<span class="property">filter</span>)(<span class="function">(<span class="params">e</span>) =&gt;</span> !!e),</span><br><span class="line">    <span class="title function_">ie</span>(dm, n9.<span class="property">APP_ACTIONS_VIA_DEEP_LINKS</span>), <span class="comment">// actually execute via dm</span></span><br><span class="line">  );</span><br><span class="line">&#125;)</span><br></pre></td></tr></table></figure><p>A <code>slack://app?action=something</code> link passes through without any confirmation.</p><p><code>dm</code> looks like this:</p><figure class="highlight jsx"><table><tr><td class="gutter"><pre><span class="line">1</span><br><span class="line">2</span><br><span class="line">3</span><br><span class="line">4</span><br><span class="line">5</span><br><span class="line">6</span><br></pre></td><td class="code"><pre><span class="line">dm = <span class="function">(<span class="params">e</span>) =&gt;</span> &#123; <span class="keyword">switch</span> (e) &#123;</span><br><span class="line">  <span class="keyword">case</span> tT.<span class="property">gM</span>.<span class="property">QUIT_APP</span>: <span class="keyword">return</span> <span class="title function_">eO</span>(); <span class="comment">// quitting app</span></span><br><span class="line">  <span class="keyword">case</span> tT.<span class="property">gM</span>.<span class="property">REVEAL_LOGS</span>: <span class="keyword">return</span> <span class="title function_">ek</span>(); <span class="comment">// download logs and open file explorer (has a confirm modal)</span></span><br><span class="line">  <span class="keyword">case</span> tT.<span class="property">gM</span>.<span class="property">RESET_WINDOW</span>: <span class="keyword">return</span> <span class="title function_">ej</span>(); <span class="comment">// reset window to restore the slack window</span></span><br><span class="line">  <span class="keyword">case</span> tT.<span class="property">gM</span>.<span class="property">CLEAR_CACHE_AND_RESTART</span>: <span class="keyword">return</span> <span class="title function_">eY</span>(); <span class="comment">// clear cache and restart</span></span><br><span class="line">&#125;&#125;</span><br></pre></td></tr></table></figure><p>It can perform these actions, and only REVEAL_LOGS requires consent.</p><hr><p>Findings</p><ol><li>Unconfirmed app actions (APP_ACTIONS_VIA_DEEP_LINKS)</li></ol><ul><li>slack:&#x2F;&#x2F;app&#x2F;?action&#x3D;quit</li><li>slack:&#x2F;&#x2F;app&#x2F;?action&#x3D;reset-window</li><li>slack:&#x2F;&#x2F;app&#x2F;?action&#x3D;clear-cache-and-restart</li></ul><p>Clicking links like these executes them without confirmation.</p><ol start="2"><li>Unconfirmed settings changes (in the allowlist, f7)</li></ol><table><thead><tr><th>Setting</th><th>Effect</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>startNetLogAtLaunch</td><td>START_NET_LOG_AT_LAUNCH checks this flag right after boot and auto-starts network capture. When it finishes, it resets back to false.</td></tr><tr><td>launchOnStartup</td><td>Auto-launches Slack on OS login (persistent).</td></tr><tr><td>releaseChannelOverride</td><td>value&#x3D;prod(default)&#x2F;beta&#x2F;dogfood. Decides which build Slack pulls via auto-update.</td></tr><tr><td>hideOnStartup</td><td>When started via auto-launch, starts hidden without showing the window.</td></tr><tr><td>runFromTray</td><td>Stays resident in the tray even when the window is closed.</td></tr><tr><td>clientEnvironment (used alone)</td><td>Changes the client trust tier (NORMAL&#x2F;RESTRICTED&#x2F;MILITARY).</td></tr></tbody></table><p>slack:&#x2F;&#x2F;settings?update&#x3D;{“launchOnStartup”:true,”hideOnStartup”:true,”runFromTray”:true}</p><p>It can be used like this.</p>]]></content>
      
      
      
